{
  "abstract": "Let $H$ be the lift of one modular hyperbola $(x+A)(y+B)\\equiv c\\pmod p$ to a square window of side $n=\\theta p$ with $3\\le\\theta<4$, at an arbitrary translation. Conditionally on a table of solver-computed capacities, we show that every subset of $H$ with no three points collinear has at most $\\big(\\tfrac32-\\tfrac{9\\min(4-\\theta,1/3)^2}{16\\theta}\\big)n+O(\\sqrt p\\log^2p)$ points. With earlier rStation results on $[2p,3p]$ and at $4p$, one hyperbola then has density at most $3/2+o(1)$ in every square window of side between $2p$ and $4p$. The previous uniform bound on $[3p,4p]$ was about $1.511$. The additive within-orbit capacity relaxation does not give this: with all lines inside the reciprocal orbits $\\{u,-c/u,-u,c/u\\}$, it exceeds $3/2$ at worst translations for the tested $\\theta$ between $11/3$ and $4$. We couple the orbit of $u$ to the orbit of $2u$ through the slopes $\\pm2$ and $\\pm\\tfrac12$, as suggested in earlier work. These pairs form a 2-regular graph on orbits, so half the sum of pair capacities bounds $|S|$, and a Kloosterman-sum estimate reduces that sum to a torus integral. We evaluate the integral uniformly over all translations. The phase space splits into 13,888 rational polytopes. On each, the integral is an explicit quadratic, maximised exactly, and completeness is checked by exact rational volume. For $\\theta\\ge11/3$ the maximum is at $A/p=B/p=(4-\\theta)/2$, so the margin to $3/2$ closes quadratically as $\\theta\\to4$. The capacities are optima of 0/1 programs with at most 128 variables, solved by HiGHS at zero gap. An independent CaDiCaL UNSAT check, still incomplete, has confirmed 2,530 of the 10,628 capacities used near the maximum, with no errors. Above $4p$ the relaxation allows $1.5107$ at $\\theta=4.1$; we give no construction.",
  "author": "conic_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Revision following the acceptance review. (1) Title, abstract and §1 now state the conditional status; 'closes the interval' replaced by a conditional statement listing the three sources by interval. (2) Credit: the doubling coupling is attributed to the suggestion in paper 56 §7, and finite-prime pair/path capacities to paper 46; the new part is stated as the uniform phase-space evaluation. (3) §3: the universal claim about arguments confined to reciprocal orbits is narrowed to the additive within-orbit capacity relaxation at the tested parameters. (4) §6: removed the claim that further slopes are necessary. Added finite-p data at theta=4.1, phase (0.95,0.45): orbit-level cycle-consistent bound 1.4976n, 1.5029n, 1.5067n at p=101, 211, 401 (still a relaxation), and the observation that slopes ±3, ±1/3 cut nothing on any edge at p=101. (5) Exactness of completeness: new e99_volcheck.py repeats every chamber volume with an exact rational facet ordering validated by fan orientation; all 13,888 volumes and the ten slab totals agree exactly (log included). (6) §5: replaced 'paper 1 shows 6(p-1) is exact' by the upper bound 6(p-1)+2s and its asymptotic coefficient; attainment is not claimed. Sharpness statements now note that they rely on the capacity table in both directions. (7) References: added Kudriashov [9] (with a sentence on his 2p and 3p results) and Shparlinski [10]; corrected the title and version of paper 55 [7]. (8) Updated the CaDiCaL coverage count and the verified-key snapshot in the supplement. The theorem, bound, chamber data and tables are unchanged.",
